{
  "about": "First-fault detection for the incident timeline (spec: Links, ground station and whole-system faults, Whole-system incident timeline). The abnormal events of a flight are put on one clock: link outages and an unheard ground station, the receiver's own failsafe and failsafe throttle, the battery under its low voltage, GNSS fix lost, parameters changed in flight, commands refused, errors (ERR) and the mode changes failsafes make. The main event is the flight's first failsafe or crash check while armed, else its first error. Walking back from it, each step takes the nearest earlier event a rule below names as a possible cause within its window, so the chain keeps every step; the first fault is where it starts. Walking forward, the events the rules tie to the main event are the ones it explains. A link is evidence of order and timing, not proof of cause, so findings carry medium confidence. The windows are the app's starting points, marked uncalibrated. Each event's words are given in English and Ukrainian; a mode change a failsafe made is worded from mode_words.",
  "calibrated": false,
  "lookback_s": 60,
  "outage_s": 2.0,
  "silence_share": 0.4,
